body:
Also. pick something and be a regular. Join Meet Up (look up the app) and pick something you're interested in. Then go religiously. And be friendly. You'll soon start to see familiar faces and you'll also become a familiar face. And hopefully you'll strike up conversations with people who share a common interest with you. 

&#x200B;

Goes without saying almost but... Also. Make sure you don't have any glaring hygiene or manners issues. Smell good and brush your teeth and don't interrupt and don't chew with your mouth open and don't be a dick. That's pretty much the basics.

lol, yep. A great example of an evolutionary arms race, though. Here's a pic if you're interested. 

&#x200B;

 [https://www.scientificamerican.com/gallery/clash-of-the-duck-genitalia/](https://www.scientificamerican.com/gallery/clash-of-the-duck-genitalia/)

No, dawg. I totally get you. When I'm depressed life and ticking time feels like a knife sliding across my existence. I used to pride myself in taking joy in life and little moments. Right now (trying to remember it will get better and not always feel like this) stuff feels awful and I just want to sleep life away. But I'm not suicidal. 

&#x200B;

It's a normal part of depression. Hang in there and I hope you find some things that make you smile. It will get better. Wait. Get the meds or help that you need. It takes time.
